  :adr/body "# ADR-2607255100: toshokan self-growing resident harvest

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-25
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed under standing authorization)

## Context

Owner asked whether any repo ingests all publicly available works worldwide for Datomic query, then directed: design + implement, ingest, resident on murakumo.cloud, persist, make the repo self-grow.

Investigation (prior turn) found:

- **No** repo holds full-text of all public works worldwide.
- Closest real base is **`kotoba-lang/toshokan`** (ADR-2607199900): national library bibliographic metadata (NDL/LOC/DNB/BnF/KB/Libris/NB/ICCU…), git journal SSoT, kotobase fold path already proven with live data.
- `product-corpus` is a Common Crawl **product** corpus (schema.org Product), not literary works.
- `global-legislation-datoms` catalogs legal sources without full text.
- Unlimited whole-web crawl and search-API proxy are already rejected (ADR-2607192200).

So the correct move is **not** a greenfield mega-crawler, but to upgrade `toshokan` into a **self-growing, resident, durable** bibliographic harvest loop.

## Decision

### 1. Scope remains metadata-only public bibliographic works

- **In**: title, creator, publisher, date, identifiers, subjects from official (or documented) national-library APIs that allow non-commercial machine access without CAPTCHA bypass.
- **Out**: full text, page images, paywalled content, bot-detection bypass, unofficial scrapers for Iran/Russia (remain `:spec`).
- \"Worldwide\" means **grow coverage across official catalogs and seed queries over time**, not a claim of complete global inventory on day one.

### 2. Self-growth of the repo itself

| artifact | growth |
|---|---|
| `seeds.edn` | hand seeds + daemon appends creator-derived seeds (capped by `:max-seeds`) |
| `80-data/public/<source>.journal.edn` | append-only quads `[entity attr value tx :add]` |
| `state.edn` | cursor, per-(source,seed) page, exhausted pairs |
| git remote | each successful tick with `--push` commits + pushes → **remote history is the growth log** |

This matches ADR-2607072300 (git journal authority) and the product-corpus self-append pattern, without importing full text into git.

### 3. Persistence dual plane

1. **Authoritative**: journal files in this repo (git).
2. **Query/index**: `scripts/kotobase-ingest-toshokan.cljs` folds into `backend.kotobase.net` graph `toshokan-library-catalog` under a self-minted did:key (existing path). Local DataScript via `scripts/query.cljs` for offline verification.

### 4. Residency on murakumo fleet host = LaunchAgent

- Label: `com.kotoba-lang.toshokan-tick`
- Entry: `~/.gftd/run-toshokan-tick.cljs` → `daemon.cljs --once --push --ingest`
- Interval: 21600s (6h) — polite to library APIs; not a realtime price loop
- **Not** murakumo WASM `on-tick` yet. ADR-2607252400 (CID capabilities for guest crawl) remains the upgrade path; LaunchAgent is the honest production path today (same as fleet-ci / itonami-qwen36 ticks).

### 5. Daemon tick algorithm

1. Load `seeds.edn` + `state.edn`
2. Pick next non-exhausted `(source × seed × page)`
3. Call live API (sequential, identifying User-Agent)
4. Dedupe by entity id already in journal
5. Append new quads
6. Grow seeds from new creators (bounded)
7. Optional git commit/push
8. Optional kotobase ingest when new entities > 0

Paging: NDL `startRecord`, LOC `sp=` for deep growth; other sources first-page until they gain start/offset.

## Consequences

(+) Owner request is answered with a **real running loop**, not a paper design: ingest, persist, query, residency, self-growth.

(+) Stays inside legal/safety floors (official APIs, metadata-only, no CAPTCHA bypass).

(+) Reuses proven fold identity and journal format — no second parallel corpus invents a competing schema.

(-) Completeness is **asymptotic**: only seeds × reachable official APIs. Korea remains key-gated; Iran/Russia remain unimplemented.

(-) Full-text public-domain corpora (Gutenberg, NDL digital, etc.) are still out of scope; if wanted, they need a separate annex/DataLad plane (large-binary skill), not journal quads of megabyte texts.

(-) LaunchAgent runs on the fleet host that has git credentials and network; it is not multi-node auctioned WASM yet.

## Alternatives rejected

| option | why not |
|---|---|
| New repo from scratch | duplicates toshokan sources + journal + fold |
| Common Crawl full-text of books | license mess, bot policy, not \"official catalog\" path; CC is page HTML not library authority |
| Immediate WASM on-tick guest | blocked on CID capability work (ADR-2607252400) |
| Full-text in git | history explosion; use annex/B2 if ever added |

## Implementation pointers

- `orgs/kotoba-lang/toshokan/scripts/daemon.cljs`
- `orgs/kotoba-lang/toshokan/scripts/query.cljs`
- `orgs/kotoba-lang/toshokan/seeds.edn`
- `orgs/kotoba-lang/toshokan/deploy/com.kotoba-lang.toshokan-tick.plist`
- `~/.gftd/run-toshokan-tick.cljs`
